   7: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   8:     """
   9:     Expand each red pixel into a clipped 3x3 blue halo while preserving existing foreground pixels.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure
  12:     A black-background grid contains one or more red marker pixels and may contain other non-red foreground markers.
  13:     Rule
  14:     For every red pixel, recolor each black cell in its Chebyshev-distance-1 neighborhood to blue; do not overwrite any existing foreground pixel.
  15:     Key insight
  16:     The red pixels are centers of independent 3x3 stamps, clipped by the grid boundary, and the stamp only fills background cells.
