   9:     Move every foreground object straight downward by a number of rows equal to its own pixel count.
  10: 
  11:     Input structure:
  12:     - The grid has one dominant background color.
  13:     - The foreground is made of separated 4-connected monochromatic objects.
  14:     - Objects may move partly below the bottom edge of the grid.
  15: 
  16:     Rule:
  17:     - Clear the canvas to the background.
  18:     - For each foreground object, compute its area in pixels.
  19:     - Redraw the object at the same columns and that many rows lower, clipping pixels below the grid.
  20: 
  21:     Key insight:
  22:     - The downward displacement is the object's own area; color and shape only identify which pixels move together.
